<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Ms. Spencer returns one week after her first visit and is seen by Dr. Rosenthal, the eating disorders psychiatrist, on the same day. She has taken potassium chloride 20 mEq twice daily without stomach upset. She has kept the self-monitoring record she was given: seven episodes of binge eating with vomiting this week, from about ten, and breakfast on three days. She has met the dietitian once. She has had no palpitations, cramps, weakness, dizziness, or blood in the vomit. Her mood is still low and she is tired, but she says that telling someone has been a relief. She has had no thoughts of suicide or self-harm. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Binge eating and vomiting</td><td>Seven episodes this week, from about ten</td></tr><tr><td>Potassium supplement</td><td>20 mEq twice daily, every dose taken</td></tr><tr><td>Regular eating</td><td>Breakfast on three days; dietitian seen once</td></tr><tr><td>Mood</td><td>Low; PHQ-9 13; item 9 scored 0</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

